WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:00.973
(light and bouncy orchestral string music)

00:00:00.973 --> 00:00:02.830
- [Narrator] About the
size of a house cat,

00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:04.360
this wily little creature

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:07.380
is the smallest fox found in the U.S.

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:10.530
But even at five pounds, they
are the largest land mammal

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:13.280
on the Channel Islands off
the coast of California.

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:16.880
This is the island fox.

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:29.300
Island foxes are descendants
of mainland gray foxes,

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.690
but have grown smaller
over thousands of years

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:34.970
to adapt to the limited
resources of their island homes.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:36.850
In recent years,

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:39.480
a chain of events caused
these little foxes

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.680
to be federally listed as endangered.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:46.830
Bald eagles once lived
harmoniously with the island fox,

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:49.130
never considering them as food.

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:49.963
But then,

00:00:49.963 --> 00:00:51.780
the less forgiving golden eagles arrived

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:53.090
in the Channel Islands,

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:55.510
and began preying upon the island fox,

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:57.740
hunting them to near extinction.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:02.270
But through a recovery program,

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:04.340
the golden eagles were relocated

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:07.160
and the island fox population
is on the rise again.

00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:10.110
This is the island fox.

